Qubits 2 and 3 start in the Bell state $(|00\rangle + |11\rangle)/\sqrt{2}$. The sender applies a CNOT from qubit 1 to qubit 2, then a Hadamard on qubit 1, and measures both. The receiver applies $X$ if the second outcome is 1 and $Z$ if the first outcome is 1.

```latex
\begin{quantikz}
\lstick{$|\psi\rangle$} & \ctrl{1} & \gate{H} & \meter{} & \cw & \cwbend{2} \\
\lstick{$|0\rangle$} & \targ{} & \ctrl{1} & \qw & \meter{} & \cwbend{1} \\
\lstick{$|0\rangle$} & \qw & \targ{} & \qw & \qw & \gate{X^{m_2} Z^{m_1}}
\end{quantikz}
```

